duramen 0.1

section OR "Running the examples through the oracle"
  text
    Every example is a claim about the program, and the oracle is the specification's model of
    it. When a record has no other errors, the checker runs every example through the oracle
    and reports where the two disagree, before any builder sees the example. The example records
    here use the oracle under Files (`fixtures/echo.mjs`), which answers with its input, or as
    its input tells it to.

open OR-001 "The oracle's standard input and output"
  text
    What kind of file the oracle's standard input and output are (pipes, sockets or regular
    files), and so what an oracle that looks at them finds. Round eleven of CONFIDENCE-3.md
    found s23 giving its oracle sockets, and s24 files that it wrote in full before starting
    the oracle. It covers records whose oracle reports the kind of its standard input or
    output, and nothing else.

open OR-002 "Where the request's files are put for the oracle"
  text
    Where the checker puts the request's files to run the oracle, and so what an oracle finds
    above the folder that holds them, the request's top folder. Round twelve of
    CONFIDENCE-3.md found s26 putting them in a folder inside its own implementation's folder,
    where an oracle that looks one folder up finds that implementation's files, and s25 in the
    system's folder for temporary files. It covers records whose oracle looks above the
    request's top folder, and nothing else.
